{{exclusive|bedrock}}
[[File:Realms Stories.png|380px|thumb|Main screen of Realms Stories]]
[[File:New UI - Updated Realms Hub Screen Menu "Community" Tab - Story Feed (Bedrock Preview 26.20.22).png|380px|thumb|Main screen of the Realms Hub{{Upcoming}}]]
'''Realms Stories''' is a social hub for members of a [[Realms|Realm]], where players can comment, share [[screenshots]], and view player activity.

The features from Realms Stories are planned to be merged with the Realm management into '''Realms Hub''' in an upcoming update.

== Usage ==
Realms Stories is available for all players that are member of a [[Realm]] in ''[[Bedrock Edition]]'', for both Realms Plus and Realms Core subscriptions. It can be accessed from the main screen of the Realm in the [[play]] screen, and also from the Edit Realm screen for the owner of the Realm. It can also be accessed from the [[Game Menu|game menu]] while playing on the Realm.

Unlike a Realms server itself, which is hosted on servers owned by [[Mojang Studios]], Realms Stories is hosted on Xbox's [[social]] network. Each Realm has a private "Club" in the Xbox Network, making all posted screenshots available from the Xbox profile page for any member, where they can also be downloaded. Because Stories is hosted on the Xbox Network, the data is slightly delayed from the actual server. Furthermore, old Stories (usually past page 9) are automatically deleted.

The main screen of Realms Stories has three tabs, and a button to open the Realms Stories settings in the top-right.

=== Realms Hub ===
Currently in ''[[Minecraft Preview]]'', Realms Stories is merged with the Realm management into the Realms Hub, except in the [[Game Menu|game menu]]. All features from Realms Stories are still available in the Hub, as well as all features from the manage Realm screens. The owner can also grant administrator rights to members which allows them to manage most settings that were previously exclusive to the owner. For the parts of Realms Hub related to the main Realm management, see {{Slink|Realms|Realms Hub}}.

== Story Feed ==
[[File:Ore UI - Realms Stories Add Story Screen Menu (Bedrock).png|thumb|Adding a story post]]
In the Story Feed, all story posts from Realm members are shown on the right side of the screen, and a list of recently played members on the left side. A player can add with the purple button on the top-left. A story post can contain text, and/or a [[screenshot]] that is stored in-game.

Every story post in the Story Feed shows the player that added the story, and the time or date when the story was added. If the story contains a screenshot, the player can open it in full screen by clicking on it. Every post can also be liked with the button below, including a player's own posts. The amount of likes is shown on the left.

Players can also comment on every story post. These comments can only include text, but they can be liked by any player in the comments screen.

With the options button on the bottom-right of a post or comment, player's can remove their own posts, or report them to Xbox Enforcement. The Realm's owner can delete any story or comment, while other members can only delete their own. Other members can also notify the Realm's owner about a story. These reports can be accessed from the Realms Stories settings for the owner, where they can delete, dismiss, or report the message. The owner can also see which members reported a message.

In the upcoming Realms Hub, the story feed is located in "Story feed" section of the "Community" tab, the first screen after opening the Hub. This functions exactly the same as Realms Stories, but members with administrator role can also delete stories. The Feed moderation from the [[Realms Stories#Realms Stories settings|Realms Stories settings]] is moved here and available for all administrators. There is also a new "Admin log" tab with currently no use.

