== Timeline ==
[[File:Ore UI - Realms Stories Screen Menu "Timeline" Tab (Bedrock).png|thumb|The "Timeline" tab]]
Realm Stories also contain a Timeline table that shows numerous activity of players in the Realm. The playing times are colored for each player. One week of playing times is shown on the screen, but older data can be viewed with the arrow buttons above. To gain access to the Timeline and store activity data, a player needs to opt in for the Timeline. Players can opt out at any time, and they can also opt in anytime later again. The Realm's owner can view all members that are opted out.

== Members ==
[[File:Ore UI - Realms Stories Screen Menu "Members" Tab (Bedrock).png|thumb|The "Members" tab]]
Shows a list of all Realm members and their activity or online status. The list can be sorted and filtered, and there is a text box on the top-left to search for members. The Realm's owner can also access the "Members" settings tab in the Manage Realm screen from here.
[[File:New UI - Realms Hub Screen Menu "Community" Tab - Members (Bedrock Preview 26.20.22).png|thumb|Members tab in the Realms Hub]]
In the upcoming Realms Hub, this list is accessed from the "Community" tab, and also shows invited players. Furthermore, the list can be filtered for Realm roles, and all players can view the permissions for each member. The Realm owner can also change the Realm roles and grant administrator permissions. The owner and administrators can manage members from here, including removing or banning them, or invite new players, manage invite links, or [[player permissions]].

== Admin log ==
{{in dev|be|section=1}}
The Admin log in the Realms Hub is accessible for administrators from the "Community" tab. Here, recent changes performed by administrators are logged. Each entry shows the date and time and administrator, as well as the specific action. This includes changes to server settings, changes to activated add-ons, and major changes to worlds on the Realm.

